        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "So when this was done, others also, which had diseases in the island, came, and were healed:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 28:9",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "Who also honoured us with many honours; and when we departed, they laded us with such things as were necessary.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 73,
            "end": 75
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 28:10",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And after three months we departed in a ship of Alexandria, which had wintered in the isle, whose sign was Castor and Pollux.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 28:11",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And landing at Syracuse, we tarried there three days.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 41
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 28:12",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "And from thence we fetched a compass, and came to Rhegium: and after one day the south wind blew, and we came the next day to Puteoli:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "GR went around, took a circuitous course."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 28:13",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "Where we found brethren, and were desired to tarry with them seven days: and so we went toward Rome.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 28:14",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "And from thence, when the brethren heard of us, they came to meet us as far as Appii forum, and The three taverns: whom when Paul saw, he thanked God, and took courage.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 138,
            "end": 145,
            "text": "TG Thanksgiving."
          },
          {
            "start": 160,
            "end": 167,
            "text": "TG Courage."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Thanksgiving.",
            "prettyString": "TG Thanksgiving",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
