          {
            "raw": "TG Courage.",
            "prettyString": "TG Courage",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Courage",
                "entryId": "tg-courage",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 28:15",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "And when we came to Rome, the centurion delivered the prisoners to the captain of the guard: but Paul was suffered to dwell by himself with a soldier that kept him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 28:16",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass, that after three days Paul called the chief of the Jews together: and when they were come together, he said unto them, Men and brethren, though I have committed nothing against the people, or customs of our fathers, yet was I delivered prisoner from Jerusalem into the hands of the Romans.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 144,
            "end": 147
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 28:17",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "Who, when they had examined me, would have let me go, because there was no cause of death in me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 49
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 28:18",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "But when the Jews spake against it, I was constrained to appeal unto Cæsar; not that I had ought to accuse my nation of.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 35
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 28:19",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "For this cause therefore have I called for you, to see you, and to speak with you: because that for the hope of Israel I am bound with this chain.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 104,
            "end": 108,
            "text": "Acts 23:6. TG Hope."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 59
          },
          {
            "start": 78,
            "end": 82
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 28:20",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "And they said unto him, We neither received letters out of Judæa concerning thee, neither any of the brethren that came shewed or spake any harm of thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 28:21",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "But we desire to hear of thee what thou thinkest: for as concerning this sect, we know that every where it is spoken against.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 28:22",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "And when they had appointed him a day, there came many to him into his lodging; to whom he expounded and testified the kingdom of God, persuading them concerning Jesus, both out of the law of Moses, and out of the prophets, from morning till evening.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 91,
            "end": 100,
            "text": "D&C 68:1."
          },
          {
            "start": 214,
            "end": 222,
            "text": "Acts 3:18 (18–21); 24:14; 26:22; Alma 18:36."
